 # oripa.xyz ($ORIPA): Prelaunch Research
+
 
 ## TL;DR
 
 Under the proposed design, $ORIPA is a **loss-mining token**. Tokens are minted along a curve only when the drawn card’s locked price is below the ticket price. In the all-melt model, **up to about 27.75% of rip revenue goes to stakers**. The project states there is no presale, VC allocation, or team allocation. Its platform allocation is the Vault, representing 28.6% of total supply, with linear releases starting in March 2027.
 
-Three judgments matter. **First, trading availability remains unconfirmed.** The original says contracts are not deployed, but this review has not independently confirmed mainnet addresses. Under the announced schedule, tokens cannot transfer before January 13, 2027. First rips are scheduled for November 25, 2026, five days after this report. BlockSec listed an audit report on November 13. The fixed version still needs to be matched to the eventual deployment. [BlockSec report page](https://blocksec.com/audit-report/oripa-contract) **Second, the initial economics are unusual.** The first $5 million of cumulative recorded losses mint at ten tokens per USDC, implying a cash minting cost of about **$0.14–0.19 per token**. With a 20% required yield, 60% staking participation, and the time assumptions explained below, the conditional model implies **around $1.30**, roughly 7–9 times the cost range. I see that model gap as an explanation for a whitelist lottery with equal spending caps. **Third, the system is reflexive.** Token-mining demand may drive rip volume, while token price, rip volume, and staking income reinforce one another in both directions.
